From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:24:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: rtkit-helper: say so when the MTP lost
 its CPU in a deep sleep

On T8132 the MTP (keyboard and trackpad) is the bootloader's: this
driver adopts its running RTKit session and has no firmware image to
load. Its sleep path assumes the coprocessor runs through a firmware-
driven suspend, which is measured on T8140 only. The MTP is one of the
SoC's wake sources, so it should keep running, but if its CPU does stop
the resume today sends AP on to a firmware that isn't there and the
keyboard and trackpad are simply dead, with nothing in the log.

After a firmware-driven resume, check the ASC's run bit first. Stopped,
say so and send nothing. With apple_rtkit_helper.wake_restart=1, also
start the firmware again the way a coprocessor whose CPU alone was
reset comes back (apple_rtkit_power_cycled_return()). That only works
if the image survived, so it stays off by default.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c | 41 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c
index 8c518ef434..ae6e5ad30a 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit-helper.c
@@ -538,10 +538,51 @@ static int __maybe_unused apple_rtkit_helper_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * This coprocessor is meant to run through a deep sleep: the MTP and the AOP are among the
+ * SoC's wake sources, and their firmware is the bootloader's, so Linux has no image to load
+ * should it be lost. Off, a lost CPU is only reported. On, the firmware is started again
+ * from where its image sits, the way a coprocessor whose CPU alone was reset comes back
+ * (apple_rtkit_power_cycled_return()); that can only work if its memory kept the image.
+ */
+static bool wake_restart;
+module_param(wake_restart, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(wake_restart,
+		 "After a deep sleep, restart a coprocessor whose CPU stopped (default off: report it)");
+
+/* After a deep sleep: false if its CPU stopped, which nothing here can undo but a restart. */
+static bool apple_rtkit_helper_wake_alive(struct apple_rtkit_helper *helper)
+{
+	u32 control;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!pm_resume_via_firmware() || !helper->ap_idle)
+		return true;
+	control = readl(helper->asc_base + APPLE_ASC_CPU_CONTROL);
+	if (control & APPLE_ASC_CPU_CONTROL_RUN)
+		return true;
+
+	/* Nothing to tell a firmware that isn't running. */
+	helper->ap_idle = false;
+	dev_err(helper->dev, "CPU stopped across the deep sleep (control %#x): firmware lost\n",
+		control);
+	if (!READ_ONCE(wake_restart))
+		return false;
+	ret = apple_rtkit_power_cycled_return(helper->rtk,
+					      helper->asc_base + APPLE_ASC_CPU_CONTROL);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(helper->dev, "restart after the deep sleep failed: %d\n", ret);
+	else
+		dev_info(helper->dev, "restarted after the deep sleep\n");
+	return false;
+}
+
 static int __maybe_unused apple_rtkit_helper_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_rtkit_helper *helper = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
+	if (!apple_rtkit_helper_wake_alive(helper))
+		return 0;
 	/* After a firmware-driven suspend's idle notice; nothing otherwise. */
 	apple_rtkit_helper_ap_on(helper);
 	if (!helper->adopted || !of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j613"))
-- 
